+# PayPal integration contract (Fogline shop)
+
+This shop talks to PayPal Orders v2 over raw REST (`lib/paypal.js`, global `fetch`),
+not the APIMatic `paypal` SDK — there is no `paypal` dependency in `package.json`.
+If that ever changes, this sheet must be rewritten from the SDK map before coding.
+
+## Operations in scope
+
+| Operation | Call | Success shape relied on |
+|---|---|---|
+| Create order | `POST /v2/checkout/orders` `{intent:"CAPTURE", purchase_units:[…]}` | `201`, body `id` |
+| Capture | `POST /v2/checkout/orders/{id}/capture` (no body) | `201`, body `status`, `purchase_units[0].{custom_id,payments.captures[0].{status,amount.{value,currency_code}}}` |
+| Get order (settle unknown / already-captured) | `GET /v2/checkout/orders/{id}` | same `purchase_units` shape as capture |
+| Verify webhook | `POST /v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature` | `200`, `verification_status:"SUCCESS"` |
+
+## Contracts
+
+- Amounts: catalog is integer cents. One converter `centsToPayPalAmount(cents)`
+  in `lib/paypal.js` (4900 → `"49.00"`, 5 → `"0.05"`). Create sends
+  `amount.value`, `breakdown.item_total.value` (equal to total) and per-item
+  `unit_amount.value`, all from the server-priced cart; browser-sent
+  price/amount/total/currency are ignored. Currency is the cart's, upper-cased (`USD`).
+- Binding: shop order is created first; its id goes in
+  `purchase_units[0].custom_id` and `invoice_id`; the PayPal order id is stored
+  as `orders.payment_reference` under a unique index.
+- Paid means captured: only a capture with status `COMPLETED` whose amount
+  (parsed exactly back to cents) and currency equal the shop order total and
+  whose `custom_id` is that shop order settles it. Approval is never payment.
+- Errors on capture: PayPal's HTTP status, `details[0].issue`, message and
+  `debug_id` win. `INSTRUMENT_DECLINED` → 402, buyer picks another method,
+  order stays pending. `ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED` / unknown outcome → GET the
+  order and settle from PayPal's record. Capture `PENDING` → 202, wait for
+  `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED`. 401/403 → 502 (our credentials), 429 → 503,
+  other 4xx → same status with PayPal's reason, 5xx → 502.
+- Webhooks: verified via verify-webhook-signature (headers + `PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID`
+  + parsed event) before any action; non-SUCCESS → 400, no change. Event ids
+  recorded once (unique); repeats → 200, no change. Only
+  `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` can settle; `CHECKOUT.ORDER.APPROVED` never does.
+- Fulfilment: exactly once via atomic claim
+  `UPDATE … SET status='paid' … WHERE id=? AND status='pending'`; only the
+  claimant calls `fulfilOrder`. No transition moves a paid/fulfilled order back.
+- Secrets: only the client id reaches the browser (`/api/paypal/config`).
